hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2831","Narrated to us Jameel ibn al-Hasan al-Jahdami, narrated to us Mahboob ibn al-Hasan, narrated to us Dawood, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn ‘Abbaas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stopped at ‘Arafaat. When he said: *“Labbayka Allaahumma labbayk”* (Here I am, O Allah, here I am), he also said: *“Innamal-khayru khayrul-aakhirah”* (Verily, all good is in the good of the Hereafter).\n\nCHAPTER:"
